# Summary of a CPU-only run of the analysis from the v1.0 release (assembled from the run's
# own logs; times are the machine's clock).
# Machine: AMD EPYC 7V12 64-Core Processor, 128 threads, 503 GB RAM, no GPU (vast.ai).
# Code: commit 24ba290. Data: NO_IMAGES=1 scripts/setup.sh; detections.tar from the release
# (sha256 checked) plus the separate yolo_yolo11n.pt_single__coco_val files.

setup: coco_val 5000 images, kitti_train 3712, kitti_val 3769, nuimages_val 16445,
       kitti_ngdet120 120, kitti_train120 120; 2.9 GB in /root/data
detections.tar: OK

Sections run one after another (scripts/run_analysis.sh, 24 workers):
[14:59:28] gate          -> results/gate.json
[15:26:12] reproduction  -> results/reproduction.json
[15:26:13] main          -> results/main.json
[15:54:29] audit         -> results/audit.json
[16:21:36] stability     -> results/stability.json (written 16:50:26)

Remaining sections started in parallel at 16:42:43 (scripts/analyze.py <section>, 12 to 16
workers each); the sequential run was stopped once stability had finished:
prompts      -> results/prompts.json      16:43:22
errors       -> results/errors.json       16:43:47
fusion       -> results/fusion.json       16:48:38
contrasts    -> results/contrasts.json    17:47:00
robustness   -> results/robustness.json   17:47:30
subgroups    -> results/subgroups.json    17:48:15
finetune     -> results/finetune.json     17:53:13
then scripts/figures.py and scripts/tables.py

COCO check printed by the gate section (measured AP, published AP):
Faster R-CNN 37.2 37.0 | RetinaNet 35.9 36.4 | FCOS 39.1 39.2 | Faster R-CNN v2 47.3 46.7
YOLO11-N 39.3 39.5 | YOLO11-M 51.3 51.5 | YOLO11-X 54.5 54.7
D-FINE-N 42.8 42.8 | D-FINE-M 52.3 52.3 | D-FINE-X 55.8 55.8
Grounding DINO-T 48.5 48.4 | MM-GDINO-T 50.4 50.4 | LLMDet-T 55.5 (paper: 55.6, trained with COCO images)
D-FINE Hugging Face port N/M/X 42.8 / 52.3 / 55.8 | YOLO11-N single-label NMS 38.7

Comparison with the results files previously committed from the GPU machine (cmp, byte for byte):
identical: main.json, reproduction.json, audit.json, stability.json, fusion.json,
           finetune.json, prompts.json, contrasts.json
new or changed by this run (analysis code at 24ba290 differs for these sections):
           gate.json (added rows), errors.json, subgroups.json, robustness.json (new)
The unified_nms entries of robustness.json come from scripts/analyze.py unified_nms, run on a
separate CPU machine from the same release.
